## Gradient Boosting

A particularly notable result is:

```text
GDP Growth
Gradient Boosting
OOS-R² = -3.4210
```

The project associates this result with severe overfitting in the small-sample environment.

## Equity Forecasting

The equity pipeline evaluates:

* HDFC Bank
* TCS
* Trent
* Larsen & Toubro
* Titan

over the **January–May 2026** out-of-sample period.

The project reports negative OOS-R² values across the five stocks and the model suite.

This highlights the difficulty of forecasting short-horizon equity prices using historical-price information alone.

## Main Finding

The central empirical observation is:

```text
More Model Complexity
        ≠
Better Out-of-Sample Forecast
```

In small, noisy datasets, strong regularization and controlled model complexity can be more useful than unrestricted flexibility.
